{"id": "EUVD-2026-71416", "enisaUuid": "ba051640-0526-3e59-89c2-d4788dce00d2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: huawei: fix missing hid_is_usb() check\n\nto_usb_interface() can only be used on a hid_device whose parent is really\nUSB; uhid can create devices that identify as being on BUS_USB, but don't\nactually have a USB parent.\nFix the use of to_usb_interface() without a hid_is_usb() check.\n\nI have verified that it is currently possible to trigger a kernel splat due\nto this bug in an ASAN build, and that this commit fixes the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:12:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66805454c01ffefc40d08a962d606cdb73644c5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9acc2463991cdb0856fdbd63fd7178102c1ed73d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cdb6b4b34d7823254f6e1b22faf56c96ac57fb9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mfj9-ch64-p8hv", "CVE-2026-80773"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01e8121a-0c12-32c9-a047-bc8f5c59b588", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e93faaca84b73431ccef029b2c8e902e5be83006 <66805454c01ffefc40d08a962d606cdb73644c5d"}, {"id": "18776b3f-9160-3423-8007-1d3ede7e5982", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "56a51588-28f8-3e47-9031-193f3faf7e79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "8054678d-8a40-318b-acfe-52dbc00997fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "b964e894-7fdc-3302-9741-30c792bcc1cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e93faaca84b73431ccef029b2c8e902e5be83006 <4cdb6b4b34d7823254f6e1b22faf56c96ac57fb9"}, {"id": "bb8387fd-672a-3025-9eeb-818b780e00b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}},